# =============================================================================
# PRE-DEADLINE WHITELIST. The repo is public, but the approach stays private
# until submissions close (Sun Nov 8, 11:59 PM AoE = Mon Nov 9, 11:59 UTC).
#
# Everything is ignored by default; only the paths re-included below are
# published. A new file or folder stays private unless it is added here.
#
# Before every push, check:   git status --ignored   and   git ls-files
# After the deadline, replace this file with a normal blacklist .gitignore.
#
# Kept private, and why:
#   CLAUDE.md, src/, plan/, data/, docs/notes/, reports/, research_notes/
#                          -> our approach, code, pre-registration, runs, notes
#   docs/incident/KEY_FACTS.md -> our analysis of the incident
#   starter/               -> which third-party repos and datasets we chose
#                             reveals the approach (and ~400 MB of clones)
#   docs/sprint/papers/*   -> PDFs (third-party copyright; related/ hints at
#                             the approach); only the index README is public
#   docs/incident/sources/, docs/sprint/external/, docs/misc./
#                          -> verbatim copies of third-party pages and reports
#   .env, .venv            -> secrets and a symlinked local interpreter
# =============================================================================

# 1. Ignore everything.
/*

# 2. Root files that are safe to publish.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

# 3. Sprint-page notes (public information from apartresearch.com).
#    A file can only be re-included if its parent folder is re-included,
#    so each level is opened, then emptied, then the safe files are re-added.
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/sprint/
/docs/sprint/*
!/docs/sprint/README.md
!/docs/sprint/0[1-7]_*.md

# Reading-list index only (no PDFs, no related/ folder).
!/docs/sprint/papers/
/docs/sprint/papers/*
!/docs/sprint/papers/README.md

# Official report template (blank, from the organizers).
!/docs/sprint/template/
/docs/sprint/template/*
!/docs/sprint/template/README.md
!/docs/sprint/template/apart_report_template.md

# 4. Safety net: these never get published, even if a rule above is loosened.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.venv
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
CLAUDE.md
**/notes/
**/data/
**/runs/
**/logs/
*.jsonl
